Read CURRENT-WORK.md and your TASKS/STATUS/HANDOFF before selecting an authorized queue item. The assignment is the acting human/workstream owner's authorized slice of the batch. Before every task/fix check human owner AND workstream plus paths/lease. Continue only for that same owner; a cross-owner next task requires STOP IMPLEMENTATION, exact tested dependency SHA, and handoff. WS3 may integrate declared commits, never automatically take WS1/WS2 code. Unavailability is not permission; reassignment needs explicit senior authority recorded in CURRENT-WORK. Review fixes return to their owner. Keep exact ownership and central leases from OWNERSHIP.md. No shared checkout or scope expansion. Canonical procedure: docs/plans/LONG-RUNNING-WORK.md (ADR-012 as amended by ADR-014; ownership-preserving section).
